silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_01_functors_as_typed_cross_kg_mappings_sections_01_household_kg_as_source_category_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'HouseholdKgAsSourceCategoryConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the concrete household cat called Mittens, identified by microchip 9, owner-fed daily, subject of household vet record 77; also, Mittens' implanted microchip's serial identifier (a 9-digit string registered with the household vet); also, the household-side aggregate vet record numbered 77, kept in the family's filing cabinet, that ties the body-mass measurement to the microchip registration." .
